    <briefdescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classHumanPlayer" kindref="compound">HumanPlayer</ref> class represents the human player in the game. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Inherits from the abstract base class <ref refid="classPlayer" kindref="compound">Player</ref>. It is responsible for capturing user input (either through GUI clicks or, in this case, through voice recognition using <ref refid="classSpeechManager" kindref="compound">SpeechManager</ref>) and converting it into a valid move on the board.</para>
<para>Uses a dedicated worker thread (<computeroutput>QThread</computeroutput>) for voice processing (<computeroutput><ref refid="classSpeechManager" kindref="compound">SpeechManager</ref></computeroutput>) to avoid blocking the main GUI thread.</para>
    </detaileddescription>
